course: dictionary
lesson: 2815
title: Distress: worry and danger
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Distress is a strong word. It means great worry, sadness or pain. «But you are evidently in sore trouble and distress, so I will not desert you.» The speaker can see that someone is very upset and in trouble, so they promise not to leave.
explain: Distress can also mean a danger where help is badly needed. A ship «in distress» is in serious trouble and needs rescue fast. A «distress signal» is a call for help, like a flare or the SOS signal.
explain: Distress can be a verb too, meaning to make someone very worried or upset. Pictures that are «distressing» upset the people who see them. The clues around the word tell you which meaning fits: worry, danger or upset.
fact: Distress means great worry, sadness or pain.
fact: «A ship in distress» means a ship that is in danger and needs help quickly.
fact: A «distress signal» is a call for help, such as SOS.
fact: In Morse code, SOS is three dots, three dashes, three dots.
fact: «Distressed jeans» are made to look old on purpose.
exercise: «In Morse code the distress signal SOS is three dots, three dashes, three dots.» What is a distress signal? | *A call for help | A type of cloud | A kind of music | A sign for a shop
exercise: «A ship in distress needs help.» What does in distress mean here? | *In serious danger and needing help | Moving very fast across the sea | Being painted a new colour | On a holiday cruise
exercise: «But you are evidently in sore trouble and distress, so I will not desert you.» What does distress mean here? | *Great worry, sadness or pain | A loud noise | A set of old clothes | A kind of boat
test: «Distressed jeans» are made to look what, on purpose? | *Old | Very clean | Brand new and shiny | Very warm
test: What does it mean to distress someone? | To give someone a present | *To make someone very worried or upset | To make someone laugh | To help someone across the road
exam: A warning says pictures «may be distressing». What does this tell you? | *The pictures could upset you, so you may want to look away | The pictures are free to see | The pictures are very short | The pictures are in colour
